#!/usr/bin/env perl

use 5.040;

our $VERSION = '0.001';
use utf8;

use English qw(-no_match_vars);
use Cwd     qw(getcwd);

use Epub::Convert::VerticalToHorizontal::CLI   qw(run_cli);
use Epub::Convert::VerticalToHorizontal::Files qw(command_arguments);

sub UTF8_CODE_PAGE () { return 65_001; }

if ( $OSNAME eq 'MSWin32' ) {
    require Win32;
    Win32::SetConsoleCP(UTF8_CODE_PAGE);
    Win32::SetConsoleOutputCP(UTF8_CODE_PAGE);
}
binmode STDOUT, ':encoding(UTF-8)'
    or die "Cannot configure standard output: $OS_ERROR\n";
binmode STDERR, ':encoding(UTF-8)'
    or die "Cannot configure standard error: $OS_ERROR\n";

my $status;
try {
    my @arguments = command_arguments();
    $status = run_cli( \@arguments, getcwd() );
}
catch ($error) {
    print {*STDERR} $error or die "Cannot print failure: $OS_ERROR\n";
    $status = 1;
}
exit $status;

__END__

=head1 NAME

epub-v2h - Preserve horizontal EPUBs and convert vertical text

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    perl epub-v2h --analyze-only
    perl epub-v2h --output-directory horizontal-perl --report-path perl-report.json
    perl epub-v2h --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Requires Perl 5.40 and dependencies declared in Makefile.PL or cpanfile.
See README.md for installation, verification and layout limitations.

=head1 USAGE

    epub-v2h --input-path book.epub --output-directory horizontal
    epub-v2h --analyze-only --json

=head1 REQUIRED ARGUMENTS

None. Without C<--input-path>, scans the current working directory.

=head1 OPTIONS

C<--input-path PATH> selects a file or nonrecursive directory.
C<--output-directory DIR> selects the output folder, defaulting to
C<horizontal/> in the current directory. C<--report-path FILE> writes JSON.
C<--analyze-only> inspects without producing books. C<--what-if> previews
without writing books, directories or reports. C<--json> selects JSON stdout;
C<--verbose> prints input paths to stderr. C<--help> prints usage.

=head1 DIAGNOSTICS

Diagnostics go to standard error. An invalid book does not stop later books.
Existing outputs and reports are rejected rather than overwritten.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

Zero for successful processing or help, one for invalid arguments, operational
failures or a batch containing at least one failed book.

=head1 CONFIGURATION

No configuration files are read. Relative paths use the working directory.
C<PERL5LIB> can select locally installed prerequisites. Windows console output
uses UTF-8, and Unicode arguments are recovered using wide Windows APIs.

=head1 DEPENDENCIES

Perl 5.40 and Epub::Convert::VerticalToHorizontal with its declared prerequisites.
Windows additionally uses the Win32 module supplied with native Windows Perl.

=head1 INCOMPATIBILITIES

Directory scans are nonrecursive. Unsupported encodings, signed or encrypted
conversion targets and malformed resources produce explicit failures.

=head1 BUGS AND LIMITATIONS

The converter changes direction declarations, not reader rendering. Consult
README.md for preservation guarantees and classification limitations.

=head1 AUTHOR

Itsuki Hayashi.

